{"seconds": 458.939, "paras": [{"n": 1, "start": 0.41, "end": 8.76, "text": "In Sunrise on the Reaping, a sixteen-year-old boy's name is ", "cut": 9.14}, {"n": 2, "start": 9.52, "end": 21.26, "text": "It's fiction. But fifty-seven years ago, America did somethi", "cut": 21.79}, {"n": 3, "start": 22.32, "end": 35.7, "text": "Sunrise on the Reaping is based on something real. And by th", "cut": 36.18}, {"n": 4, "start": 36.66, "end": 46.25, "text": "Welcome to the Fiction Files. I'm your Detective. Every stor", "cut": 47.08}, {"n": 5, "start": 47.91, "end": 63.43, "text": "First, the fiction. In Panem, every child aged twelve to eig", "cut": 63.86}, {"n": 6, "start": 64.29, "end": 75.94, "text": "In Sunrise on the Reaping, it's even worse. It's the fiftiet", "cut": 76.37}, {"n": 7, "start": 76.8, "end": 88.59, "text": "But here's the detail most people forget. The reaping isn't ", "cut": 89.02}, {"n": 8, "start": 89.45, "end": 94.22, "text": "So the poorest kids have the worst odds. Remember that. It's", "cut": 94.75}, {"n": 9, "start": 95.28, "end": 106.44, "text": "Suzanne Collins has said the idea came to her one night whil", "cut": 106.87}, {"n": 10, "start": 107.3, "end": 113.63, "text": "She's also said she loved the Greek myth of Theseus, where A", "cut": 114.06}, {"n": 11, "start": 114.49, "end": 118.11, "text": "That's the version everyone's heard. Here's the one nobody t", "cut": 118.74}, {"n": 12, "start": 119.37, "end": 132.63, "text": "It's 1969. America is deep in the Vietnam War, and the army ", "cut": 133.06}, {"n": 13, "start": 133.49, "end": 136.44, "text": "So the government tries something new. A lottery.", "cut": 136.92}, {"n": 14, "start": 137.4, "end": 151.21, "text": "On the evening of December the first, 1969, at the headquart", "cut": 151.64}, {"n": 15, "start": 152.07, "end": 158.09, "text": "It's for men born between 1944 and 1950. And it's broadcast ", "cut": 158.52}, {"n": 16, "start": 158.95, "end": 165.74, "text": "A congressman named Alexander Pirnie reaches in and pulls ou", "cut": 166.17}, {"n": 17, "start": 166.6, "end": 171.61, "text": "If you were born on September the fourteenth, you are now nu", "cut": 172.14}, {"n": 18, "start": 172.67, "end": 183.0, "text": "One by one, the dates come out and go up on a board. Across ", "cut": 183.43}, {"n": 19, "start": 183.86, "end": 188.96, "text": "In the end, every man whose birthday came out in the first o", "cut": 189.49}, {"n": 20, "start": 190.02, "end": 199.18, "text": "Now, pause the video for a second. Find your birthday on thi", "cut": 200.31}, {"n": 21, "start": 201.44, "end": 213.2, "text": "To be clear, Suzanne Collins has never said this lottery ins", "cut": 213.78}, {"n": 22, "start": 214.36, "end": 215.69, "text": "But that's not the strangest part.", "cut": 216.22}, {"n": 23, "start": 216.75, "end": 221.26, "text": "Remember how the reaping isn't fair? The 1969 lottery wasn't", "cut": 221.69}, {"n": 24, "start": 222.12, "end": 232.08, "text": "The capsules had been put into the container month by month,", "cut": 232.51}, {"n": 25, "start": 232.94, "end": 250.54, "text": "So if you were born late in the year, you were more likely t", "cut": 250.97}, {"n": 26, "start": 251.4, "end": 259.6, "text": "In Panem, being poor put your name in the bowl more times. I", "cut": 260.28}, {"n": 27, "start": 260.96, "end": 262.85, "text": "Now here's where this case gets personal.", "cut": 263.38}, {"n": 28, "start": 263.91, "end": 275.61, "text": "Suzanne Collins's father was an officer in the United States", "cut": 276.04}, {"n": 29, "start": 276.47, "end": 283.94, "text": "She later wrote a picture book about that year, called Year ", "cut": 284.37}, {"n": 30, "start": 284.8, "end": 300.83, "text": "Collins has said her father felt it was his job to make sure", "cut": 301.26}, {"n": 31, "start": 301.69, "end": 309.54, "text": "So the woman who wrote the most famous story about children ", "cut": 310.27}, {"n": 32, "start": 311.0, "end": 315.18, "text": "And there's one more piece of evidence. It's the key to Sunr", "cut": 315.61}, {"n": 33, "start": 316.04, "end": 327.459, "text": "When Collins announced the book, she said it was inspired by", "cut": 327.889}, {"n": 34, "start": 328.319, "end": 345.329, "text": "Hume's question was simple. Why do millions of people let a ", "cut": 345.759}, {"n": 35, "start": 346.189, "end": 358.929, "text": "Even the country's name is a clue. Panem comes from an old R", "cut": 359.509}, {"n": 36, "start": 360.089, "end": 363.229, "text": "Now look at what happened in America in the weeks before the", "cut": 363.659}, {"n": 37, "start": 364.089, "end": 374.479, "text": "On November the third, 1969, President Nixon went on televis", "cut": 374.909}, {"n": 38, "start": 375.339, "end": 382.729, "text": "Twelve days later, hundreds of thousands of people marched o", "cut": 383.159}, {"n": 39, "start": 383.589, "end": 387.579, "text": "Sixteen days after that, the lottery was drawn on live TV.", "cut": 388.259}, {"n": 40, "start": 388.939, "end": 401.449, "text": "The many, and the few. Some people stayed silent. Some peopl", "cut": 402.129}, {"n": 41, "start": 402.809, "end": 404.839, "text": "So, let's look at the evidence.", "cut": 405.269}, {"n": 42, "start": 405.699, "end": 426.859, "text": "A real government really did draw young people's birthdays f", "cut": 427.289}, {"n": 43, "start": 427.719, "end": 435.889, "text": "There's no real arena. No real tributes fighting to the deat", "cut": 436.469}, {"n": 44, "start": 437.049, "end": 441.719, "text": "So, how real is Sunrise on the Reaping? The evidence says\u2026 e", "cut": 442.499}, {"n": 45, "start": 443.279, "end": 457.589, "text": "Case closed. Don't forget to tell me your 1969 number in the", "cut": 458.939}], "words": [["in", 0.46, 1], ["sunrise", 0.62, 1], ["on", 1.06, 1], ["the", 1.23, 1], ["reaping", 1.45, 1], ["a", 2.35, 1], ["sixteen", 2.46, 1], ["year", 2.88, 1], ["old", 3.14, 1], ["boy's", 3.35, 1], ["name", 3